=== PARITY (vs web CronParser.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> the web source's ONLY hook is `useTranslation`; it is a pure, synchronous, local
    tool (two `useMemo`s over `expr`) with NO data hook, NO network, NO cache. The native parity binds
    through a local P1/S8 state holder (CronParserModel) that owns `expression` and DERIVES the render
    state on read (the @Observable analogue of the web `useMemo`, memoized on the expression so the
    one-year minute scan runs at most once per edit — exactly the web `useMemo([parts])` cadence). The
    view performs no HTTP — there is none to perform.
  Engine -> CronSchedule is a faithful port of helpers.ts:
      describe()   = describeCron (the min/hr ladder, padStart(2,'0'), day/month/weekday clauses,
                     days[idx] ?? dow fallback). Output is algorithm text the web renders untranslated.
      nextRuns()   = getNextCronRuns (seconds dropped + start one minute ahead, minute-by-minute scan,
                     525960 safety bound, weekday converted from Calendar 1..7 to web getDay 0..6).
      matchField() = the inner matchField (branch order *, /, ',', '-', else exact) with JavaScript
                     parseInt (leading-digit) and Number (whole-string, ''->0) coercion reproduced so
                     malformed fields behave identically (e.g. NaN range bound -> no match, step 0 ->
                     no match). Verified by executed XCTest against a fixed UTC clock (every-minute
                     consecutive minutes, daily-midnight next-day, weekly-Sunday weekday resolution).
  Composition -> ToolCard-style header (green `timer` glyph = web lucide `Timer` + color "green" ->
    TSIconBox success tone, title + description) · monospaced expression input with a leading `timer`
    glyph + verbatim example prompt (web `Input` label + icon + placeholder) · wrapping preset bar
    (web flex-wrap ghost `Button`s -> TSButton .ghost .small in an adaptive LazyVGrid) · description
    panel (web emerald block -> success-tone summary) · next-runs list (web `Badge variant="info"` +
    `font-mono` timestamp -> info capsule + mono caption) · idle / incomplete / no-runs states.
  Shared components -> TSButton (Components/UI/Buttons) for the presets; TSIconBox (Components/UI/Badges)
    for the header chip; ContentUnavailableView for the empty states; everything else composed from the
    P1/S9 design tokens (Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius). The reusable native `ToolCard` is a
    separate surface (prompt 0010), so the card chrome is composed inline here (matching the 0011
    Base64Tool precedent) and the surface owns its own `view.opened` slug. Recharts -> none / Leaflet ->
    none (no chart/map).
  States (all render) -> the web shows output only when `parts.length === 5` (it hides everything
    otherwise) and hides the next-runs block when empty. Reproduced + expanded so no surface is a blank
    box, each with a #if DEBUG preview and tests:
      • idle        (empty input)            -> friendly ContentUnavailableView guidance.
      • incomplete  (non-empty, != 5 fields) -> "five fields required" hint (carries the field count).
      • parsed      (5 fields)               -> description panel + next-runs list.
      • no-runs     (5 fields, impossible schedule) -> subtle note instead of a hidden block.
    The generic loading / error / stale / offline states from the prompt's checklist have NO trigger on
    this surface: it is a synchronous local transform with no async data source (no spinner), no
    freshness window (nothing can be stale), and no network dependency (it works fully offline by
    nature). Reproducing them would fabricate behavior absent from the web spec; parity = matching the
    source, so they are intentionally omitted (Honesty rule 3: the source was read end-to-end; these
    branches genuinely do not exist).
  i18n -> all 10 source `t()` keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade (CronStrings, table "CronParser")
    with the web `t(key, default)` fallback: Cron Parser, Cron Parser Desc, Cron Expression, Every
    Minute / Hour / Day / Week / Month, Description, Next Runs -> ALL present in CronParser.strings, plus
    7 native chrome/a11y keys (cron.empty.*, cron.incomplete.*, cron.noRuns, cron.a11y.idle/incomplete).
    No English literals in native code (every UI string from the facade; the cron DESCRIPTION text and
    the example prompt are computed/data, rendered verbatim — the web emits them untranslated too).
  a11y -> the header is a combined header element; the input carries an accessibilityLabel (leading
    glyph hidden); preset buttons are TSButtons; run rows combine the sequence badge + timestamp; the
    surface exposes CronParserAccessibility.summary (state-aware: idle / incomplete / description +
    run count) as its combined VoiceOver label. Dynamic Type via tokens; no motion to respect.
  Telemetry -> CronParserModel.start() emits viewOpened(surface: "CronParser") exactly once via the
    P1/S11 seam (OSLog default; production injects the shared Telemetry.track(.screenView) adapter).
    Asserted by a spy test (fires once across two start() calls; slug == "CronParser").

